1
00:02:31,017 --> 00:02:41,017
All pirates searching for the treasure One Piece must brave the second half of the Grand Line.

2
00:02:41,017 --> 00:02:45,017
These wild and dangerous seas are known as the New World.

3
00:02:45,017 --> 00:02:52,017
Gold Roger and his crew were the only men to ever chart these waters and learn all the secrets they held.

4
00:02:52,017 --> 00:02:58,017
For the rest of the pirates of the world, this has proven to be the end of the road, a graveyard of dreams.

5
00:02:58,017 --> 00:03:09,017
Now, Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber after eating the gum gum fruit, sent sail into the New World with his faithful crew.

6
00:03:09,017 --> 00:03:13,017
I'm gonna be the king of the pirates!

7
00:03:16,017 --> 00:03:25,017
During their journey to the New World, Luffy and his crew arrive on Fishman Island, which is located 10,000 meters below sea level.

8
00:03:25,017 --> 00:03:33,017
The Fishman pirates, led by Hordy Jones and assisted by Vander Decken, plot to overthrow King Neptune.

9
00:03:33,017 --> 00:03:37,017
It's not long before the Straw Hats get pulled into the conflict.

10
00:03:37,017 --> 00:03:48,017
After traveling to the sea forest and meeting with Jinbe, Luffy and his crew learn of the tumultuous history of Fishman Island that, even today, continues to shape the kingdom.

11
00:03:48,017 --> 00:04:00,017
Kizaru appears! A trap to catch Tiger!

12
00:04:00,017 --> 00:04:05,017
And that's what started it all.

13
00:04:05,017 --> 00:04:11,017
Fisher Tiger's attack on the Holy Land of Marie Joie and the formation of the Sun Pirates.

14
00:04:11,017 --> 00:04:18,017
These momentous events, they shape the future of my people.

15
00:04:18,017 --> 00:04:37,017
It's hard to believe he really went through with it.

16
00:04:37,017 --> 00:04:46,017
His actions have only created more problems for Fishman Island.

17
00:04:46,017 --> 00:04:50,017
It will be quite some time before we'll welcome back to the World Summit.

18
00:04:50,017 --> 00:04:53,017
I don't even know where to begin to fix this.

19
00:04:53,017 --> 00:04:59,017
But we share the blame. Remember, we just couldn't bring ourselves to stop him.

20
00:04:59,017 --> 00:05:05,017
Tell me, why are you so adamant about this? What did you see on your trip?

21
00:05:05,017 --> 00:05:07,017
I saw human nature.

22
00:05:07,017 --> 00:05:14,017
Because I understood the depth of his suffering. The scream of his soul. It was unbearable.

23
00:05:14,017 --> 00:05:16,017
Hmm...

24
00:05:16,017 --> 00:05:31,017
Extra! Extra! Read all about it!

25
00:05:31,017 --> 00:05:36,017
Wow, he's such a badass. Fighting the Celestial Dragons? Talk about balls.

26
00:05:36,017 --> 00:05:39,017
Yeah, that makes it official! Fisher Tiger is a true hero!

27
00:05:39,017 --> 00:05:42,017
Whoa! A Fishman's gonna wind up in the history books!

28
00:05:42,017 --> 00:05:44,017
Listen, gather around!

29
00:05:44,017 --> 00:05:47,017
Hey! It's Queen Otohime!

30
00:05:47,017 --> 00:05:48,017
What is it now?

31
00:05:48,017 --> 00:05:51,017
We have cowered, and hid, and run, and yet for what?

32
00:05:51,017 --> 00:05:56,017
What have we gained from this? What good has this path done for our people?

33
00:05:56,017 --> 00:06:00,017
We can't simply turn our backs on the entire world to cut off all humans.

34
00:06:00,017 --> 00:06:04,017
It will doom us. Some humans are bad, yes, but not all of them.

35
00:06:04,017 --> 00:06:08,017
Now, we must learn to live in harmony with humanity.

36
00:06:08,017 --> 00:06:13,017
And together we can grow with them, under the bright nourishing sun.

37
00:06:13,017 --> 00:06:15,017
Grow with them, huh?

38
00:06:15,017 --> 00:06:17,017
Yeah, that's just too much to ask.

39
00:06:17,017 --> 00:06:19,017
Hey! You two!

40
00:06:22,017 --> 00:06:23,017
Sign here!

41
00:06:23,017 --> 00:06:25,017
But, but I can't! I'm sorry!

42
00:06:25,017 --> 00:06:30,017
Please, the whole island. Tiger's a hero to us for what he did, you know?

43
00:06:30,017 --> 00:06:38,017
It's just, we know his actions might turn the humans against us. But, it's their fault. They brought it on themselves. So, we can't sign.

44
00:06:38,017 --> 00:06:48,017
I know how you feel, but in seven years, or even fifteen years, you have to think about that future. There will come a day when we will be able to participate in the World Summit again.

45
00:06:49,017 --> 00:06:53,017
You have to sign! For our future! I'm begging you!

46
00:06:53,017 --> 00:07:03,017
I'm telling you, Fisher Tiger gets it! This is how you represent the Fishman District! He went head to head with the Celestial Dragons. And, he freaking won!

47
00:07:04,017 --> 00:07:06,017
Way to stick it to those disgusting humans.

48
00:07:06,017 --> 00:07:11,017
It's just like Arlong used to say, the only good human is a dead one!

49
00:07:11,017 --> 00:07:12,017
Kill, kill!

50
00:07:12,017 --> 00:07:14,017
Yeah, now put him in their place!

51
00:07:14,017 --> 00:07:22,017
The Sun Pirates are so cool! I mean, sailing the sea, and slamming the docent down on every dumb human they meet! It's awesome!

52
00:07:22,017 --> 00:07:27,017
You know what? If we were a little stronger, then I bet, we could join them!

53
00:07:27,017 --> 00:07:34,017
We'll get strong! Then, we will! Take back the sea, Sun Pirates! Kill all those worthless humans!

54
00:07:35,017 --> 00:07:36,017
Yeah!

55
00:07:36,017 --> 00:07:51,017
Hey, boss! Boss, there's an enemy ship! Boss! Hey! Hey, guys! Did you hear me? We got a crisis!

56
00:07:52,017 --> 00:07:58,017
Shut up, Hachi! Crap! Calm down! Just tell us what's going on!

57
00:07:59,017 --> 00:08:01,017
Well, this is troubling. Is it the Navy?

58
00:08:01,017 --> 00:08:03,017
Must be! They were flying their flag out there!

59
00:08:03,017 --> 00:08:06,017
Alright, what's next?

60
00:08:10,017 --> 00:08:11,017
What?

61
00:08:11,017 --> 00:08:14,017
There's no mistake! Those are the Sun Pirates!

62
00:08:14,017 --> 00:08:16,017
Kill Fisher Tiger!

63
00:08:20,017 --> 00:08:23,017
Ha ha ha ha! Real nice aim there!

64
00:08:28,017 --> 00:08:29,017
Fire!

65
00:08:33,017 --> 00:08:35,017
What are you doing?! Shoot them dead!

66
00:08:35,017 --> 00:08:36,017
We're trying, but they're swimming too fast!

67
00:08:36,017 --> 00:08:37,017
We're trying, but they're swimming too fast!

68
00:08:37,017 --> 00:08:40,017
We're trying, but they're swimming too fast!

69
00:08:40,017 --> 00:08:43,017
Ha ha ha ha ha ha!

70
00:08:43,017 --> 00:09:01,317
Pardon me, gents.

71
00:09:02,697 --> 00:09:04,537
You fishman bastards!

72
00:09:05,097 --> 00:09:06,797
Return the slaves, damn it!

73
00:09:07,117 --> 00:09:07,617
Surrender!

74
00:09:08,297 --> 00:09:10,697
If you play ball, they'll drop the charges!

75
00:09:10,697 --> 00:09:13,197
We're... we're Admiral!

76
00:09:13,677 --> 00:09:16,377
They're... they're bursting up through the bottom of the ship!

77
00:09:16,537 --> 00:09:16,917
What?

78
00:09:24,497 --> 00:09:25,597
You fools!

79
00:09:26,117 --> 00:09:27,977
Give us back the slaves and this will end!

80
00:09:27,977 --> 00:09:30,857
Do you even realize the serious crime you've committed?

81
00:09:31,117 --> 00:09:32,577
How dare you turn on humans!

82
00:09:32,897 --> 00:09:34,977
Know your place, you disgusting fishman!

83
00:09:35,657 --> 00:09:36,737
What was that?

84
00:09:37,537 --> 00:09:38,737
Go on now.

85
00:09:38,737 --> 00:09:41,237
Let's hear you say that again!

86
00:09:43,277 --> 00:09:45,197
Please, somebody help me.

87
00:09:47,897 --> 00:09:52,097
So slavery's perfectly legal, but freeing slaves is a crime?

88
00:09:52,897 --> 00:09:55,677
And Queen Otohime thinks you deserve a chance.

89
00:09:56,057 --> 00:09:57,457
Not that you'd give us one.

90
00:09:57,457 --> 00:10:01,817
Now, fire!

91
00:10:01,817 --> 00:10:02,297
Uh...

92
00:10:02,297 --> 00:10:02,577
ányye, you're smutting the slaves.

93
00:10:02,577 --> 00:10:03,417
YouTF?

94
00:10:03,417 --> 00:10:04,037
Now!

95
00:10:04,037 --> 00:10:04,657
Fire!

96
00:10:04,657 --> 00:10:04,917
Test到 consciousness.

97
00:10:04,917 --> 00:10:05,057
atomic戴 PDF

98
00:10:05,057 --> 00:10:05,737
Now!

99
00:10:05,737 --> 00:10:05,757
Fire!

100
00:10:06,197 --> 00:10:06,757
Blow him to pieces, men.

101
00:10:06,757 --> 00:10:07,237
Blew him to pieces!

102
00:10:07,857 --> 00:10:10,237
We know that you're hiding the slaves!

103
00:10:10,317 --> 00:10:19,997
And now, you're going to die for the havoc you've wrought!

104
00:10:19,997 --> 00:10:23,497
Blow him to pieces, men. We know that you're hiding the slaves.

105
00:10:23,777 --> 00:10:26,797
And now you're going to die for the havoc you've wrought.

106
00:10:29,677 --> 00:10:31,137
Oh, what the hell?

107
00:10:31,517 --> 00:10:32,797
These slaves you mentioned.

108
00:10:33,657 --> 00:10:35,477
He's... he's a monster.

109
00:10:45,977 --> 00:10:49,417
What proof do you possibly have that we're hiding them on board?

110
00:10:49,997 --> 00:10:52,017
Go on and check all of us if you want to.

111
00:10:52,277 --> 00:10:55,657
But from what I understand, these slaves should have a brand on them.

112
00:10:56,017 --> 00:10:57,577
Do you see that mark on any of us?

113
00:10:57,937 --> 00:11:00,117
Wait, stop! Put me down!

114
00:11:01,617 --> 00:11:02,677
Help me!

115
00:11:10,177 --> 00:11:12,397
I won't kill you. Don't worry.

116
00:11:12,937 --> 00:11:14,657
I'm not a savage like you.

117
00:11:15,957 --> 00:11:19,597
All right, guys. Take all their money and food and get back to the ship.

118
00:11:19,997 --> 00:11:25,997
Being human is a sin.

119
00:11:26,237 --> 00:11:29,637
And so, you were born deserving execution.

120
00:11:31,177 --> 00:11:32,437
No, stop!

121
00:11:32,817 --> 00:11:33,697
Drop dead!

122
00:11:33,697 --> 00:11:43,397
Vice Admiral, Rear Admiral Cutter from the G-2 branch has been defeated.

123
00:11:44,557 --> 00:11:45,117
Huh?

124
00:11:45,497 --> 00:11:47,097
Why did he engage them?

125
00:11:47,837 --> 00:11:50,957
I only wanted to report on their current whereabouts.

126
00:11:51,257 --> 00:11:53,337
If you get close enough to see them,

127
00:11:53,597 --> 00:11:57,717
well, that's apparently all it takes before their entire crew surrounds you in the water.

128
00:11:57,717 --> 00:12:02,037
Oh, scary. Fishman. Guess we should have expected that.

129
00:12:02,037 --> 00:12:07,017
Okay, do you have any intel you can share?

130
00:12:07,137 --> 00:12:10,757
Well, the way it looks, Arlong and his men are part of the crew,

131
00:12:11,097 --> 00:12:15,417
and they were responsible for the raids in the area surrounding Fishman Island.

132
00:12:16,097 --> 00:12:20,337
But we have yet to fight them on land, so it's hard to tell how strong they are.

133
00:12:20,337 --> 00:12:24,537
Arlong. Right, I've heard of him.

134
00:12:25,637 --> 00:12:27,837
There's another dangerous one on their crew.

135
00:12:28,417 --> 00:12:31,117
He's as big as Fisher Tiger and just as brutal.

136
00:12:31,537 --> 00:12:32,557
Didn't catch his name.

137
00:12:33,277 --> 00:12:35,677
Well, sounds like a real mess.

138
00:12:37,257 --> 00:12:38,677
Ow! That hurt!

139
00:12:38,677 --> 00:12:42,277
What's the big deal?

140
00:12:42,637 --> 00:12:46,317
Why the hell do you care if we kill one or two of those inferior creatures?

141
00:12:48,157 --> 00:12:51,117
It's not about them. You're both going too far.

142
00:12:51,837 --> 00:12:54,297
Look, we're not a group of killers. We're better than that.

143
00:12:54,877 --> 00:12:56,017
And don't you forget it.

144
00:12:56,357 --> 00:12:59,217
But, look, brother. Sorry, I mean boss.

145
00:12:59,557 --> 00:13:01,597
These humans have no such compunction.

146
00:13:01,817 --> 00:13:03,517
They are actively out to kill you.

147
00:13:03,777 --> 00:13:05,077
So can you blame us?

148
00:13:05,077 --> 00:13:07,937
Of course we might go too far from time to time.

149
00:13:07,937 --> 00:13:09,077
We're mad!

150
00:13:09,477 --> 00:13:10,957
Do you want to be like the humans?

151
00:13:11,537 --> 00:13:13,917
Killing someone is to kill a part of your own soul.

152
00:13:14,417 --> 00:13:17,057
We are not seeking revenge for the discrimination here.

153
00:13:17,757 --> 00:13:19,897
And that's not what Marie Joie was about either.

154
00:13:20,417 --> 00:13:22,857
I might have broken that stupid unspoken rule,

155
00:13:22,997 --> 00:13:24,817
but I only did it to free those slaves.

156
00:13:25,437 --> 00:13:28,257
The Sun Pirates are driven by the idea of liberation and freedom,

157
00:13:28,757 --> 00:13:29,917
not spiteful retribution.

158
00:13:31,197 --> 00:13:34,657
Seeking vengeance against the humans only creates a vicious cycle.

159
00:13:35,717 --> 00:13:37,197
Violence begets violence,

160
00:13:37,197 --> 00:13:39,737
and I will not be responsible for more tragedy.

161
00:13:40,417 --> 00:13:44,717
We'll end up condemning the next generation of fishmen to war with humanity.

162
00:13:46,397 --> 00:13:47,617
Can't you see that?

163
00:13:48,257 --> 00:13:50,857
We will fight and rob those who come after us,

164
00:13:51,017 --> 00:13:52,777
but we won't cross the line.

165
00:13:53,497 --> 00:13:56,337
We will not become killers.

166
00:13:56,337 --> 00:14:05,537
Listen, brother, I think you're overlooking one simple fact.

167
00:14:05,997 --> 00:14:08,617
Violence always begets violence, you say?

168
00:14:09,197 --> 00:14:10,637
Well, not if they're all dead.

169
00:14:10,797 --> 00:14:12,917
Who's going to fight back if we kill them?

170
00:14:13,737 --> 00:14:18,237
We'll massacre the animals and force all the women and children to watch,

171
00:14:18,237 --> 00:14:21,657
terrifying the idea of revenge right out of their minds.

172
00:14:22,237 --> 00:14:25,957
All we have to do is show them how powerful and ruthless we can be,

173
00:14:26,297 --> 00:14:28,997
and then they'll be paralyzed with terror.

174
00:14:29,417 --> 00:14:30,237
They will never...

175
00:14:30,797 --> 00:14:32,537
What the hell is your problem?

176
00:14:32,537 --> 00:14:33,537
What is your problem?

177
00:14:48,677 --> 00:14:49,537
What is your problem?

178
00:14:49,537 --> 00:15:13,997
That you, Jinbei?

179
00:15:13,997 --> 00:15:29,997
Arlong's a hothead who seems to strive to make a nuisance of himself.

180
00:15:29,997 --> 00:15:36,997
I don't blame him. Truth is, I've got no right to cast any judgment on the guy.

181
00:15:36,997 --> 00:15:39,997
I didn't mean...

182
00:15:39,997 --> 00:15:44,997
Jinbei, it's great what Queen Otohime's trying to accomplish.

183
00:15:44,997 --> 00:15:50,997
Though understandably, to her, there's no difference between Arlong and me.

184
00:15:50,997 --> 00:16:06,997
Honestly, there's only one thing that I'm really afraid of. My own mind.

185
00:16:06,997 --> 00:16:19,997
It's taken me all these years to understand why he told me that. What he meant.

186
00:16:19,997 --> 00:16:21,997
Up ahead! There's a pirate ship!

187
00:16:21,997 --> 00:16:23,997
Looks like a big one.

188
00:16:23,997 --> 00:16:26,997
I'm guessing they want to take us on to prove themselves.

189
00:16:26,997 --> 00:16:28,997
We are really racking up the enemies.

190
00:16:28,997 --> 00:16:33,997
Well, I say we seek their ship. Best to make an example of them.

191
00:16:33,997 --> 00:16:39,997
We were engaged in combat on a daily basis. Criminals hunted by the world government.

192
00:16:39,997 --> 00:16:45,997
Meanwhile, Queen Otohime waged her own stubborn form of battle against the world.

193
00:16:45,997 --> 00:16:46,997
Sign here!

194
00:16:46,997 --> 00:16:50,997
No, we won't! We don't want to live with humans!

195
00:16:50,997 --> 00:16:51,997
Please sign!

196
00:16:51,997 --> 00:16:56,997
Hey! The government put out a bounty on Boss Tai and Jinbei!

197
00:16:57,997 --> 00:16:58,997
Seriously?

198
00:16:58,997 --> 00:17:01,997
Wow, 230 million bearings!

199
00:17:01,997 --> 00:17:04,997
Jinbei's got 76 million on his head!

200
00:17:04,997 --> 00:17:08,997
Wanted posters! Look, they raised the reward on them again!

201
00:17:08,997 --> 00:17:11,997
Even the world government is scared of them.

202
00:17:11,997 --> 00:17:14,997
Yeah, yeah! They're gonna sink the entire navy!

203
00:17:14,997 --> 00:17:17,997
I need you to sign it!

204
00:17:17,997 --> 00:17:19,997
Let me go, your majesty!

205
00:17:19,997 --> 00:17:23,997
The next three years unfolded in a similar manner.

206
00:17:23,997 --> 00:17:27,997
And then one day, we came across a young girl on an island.

207
00:17:27,997 --> 00:17:30,997
Mister, we could use your help or something.

208
00:17:30,997 --> 00:17:31,997
Hmm?

209
00:17:31,997 --> 00:17:35,997
This girl here, she escaped from Marie Joie with the rest of us

210
00:17:35,997 --> 00:17:38,997
back when you liberated us from slavery three years ago.

211
00:17:39,997 --> 00:17:41,997
Here, look.

212
00:17:41,997 --> 00:17:48,997
She hasn't seen her parents in many years, and her home's far away.

213
00:17:48,997 --> 00:17:51,997
We would like to help. I'm sure they miss her.

214
00:17:51,997 --> 00:17:54,997
But it's highly doubtful we can safely cross the ocean.

215
00:17:55,997 --> 00:17:58,997
I'm Koala, and I'm 11 years old.

216
00:17:58,997 --> 00:18:02,997
Thanks for saving me. I'll do my best not to cause you any more trouble.

217
00:18:02,997 --> 00:18:06,997
I know she's a kid, but she's still a disgusting human.

218
00:18:06,997 --> 00:18:09,997
Why the hell would you let her on board with us?

219
00:18:09,997 --> 00:18:10,997
Just drop it, Orlong.

220
00:18:11,997 --> 00:18:13,997
I'll drop this ugly brat!

221
00:18:13,997 --> 00:18:14,997
Quit smiling, dammit!

222
00:18:14,997 --> 00:18:15,997
Orlong, no!

223
00:18:18,997 --> 00:18:19,997
Calm down!

224
00:18:19,997 --> 00:18:22,997
Let go, Hachi! I'm not done yet!

225
00:18:22,997 --> 00:18:23,997
Who's right?

226
00:18:23,997 --> 00:18:26,997
It is creepy how she won't stop smiling.

227
00:18:29,997 --> 00:18:32,997
Huh?

228
00:18:32,997 --> 00:18:33,997
You...

229
00:18:37,997 --> 00:18:38,997
What are you...

230
00:18:38,997 --> 00:18:39,997
Are you...

231
00:18:39,997 --> 00:18:40,997
I'm sorry. I'm a hard worker.

232
00:18:40,997 --> 00:18:43,997
I'll clean, and I don't need to take a break.

233
00:18:43,997 --> 00:18:44,997
So please don't hit me.

234
00:18:45,997 --> 00:18:46,997
I'm sorry.

235
00:18:47,997 --> 00:18:48,997
I'm sorry.

236
00:18:48,997 --> 00:18:49,997
I'll give it my best.

237
00:18:50,997 --> 00:18:51,997
Stop.

238
00:18:52,997 --> 00:18:53,997
I'm sorry.

239
00:18:53,997 --> 00:18:54,997
I'm sorry.

240
00:18:54,997 --> 00:18:55,997
I'll clean it.

241
00:18:56,997 --> 00:18:57,997
You're bleeding.

242
00:18:58,997 --> 00:18:59,997
I'm sorry.

243
00:18:59,997 --> 00:19:01,997
I promise that I'll never cry.

244
00:19:01,997 --> 00:19:03,997
Just please don't kill me.

245
00:19:03,997 --> 00:19:04,997
Hmm?

246
00:19:07,997 --> 00:19:08,997
It's alright.

247
00:19:08,997 --> 00:19:09,997
Are you...

248
00:19:09,997 --> 00:19:10,997
scared of us?

249
00:19:10,997 --> 00:19:11,997
